namespace Magma

/-- A member of the class, as the `4` orbit values it takes together with the proof that they name
one. `Magma.tupOK` is three tests: every orbit value is one the group's action allows, the operation
the tuple builds really is invariant, and no excess permutation is an automorphism of it. -/
@[reducible] def tup9R303 : Type := {w : Fin 4 → Fin 9 // Magma.tupOK S9R303.E S9R303.tr S9R303.z S9R303.st S9R303.X w = true}

/-- The class, as a family of magmas indexed by its own membership test. -/
@[implicit_reducible]
def srch9R303 (v : tup9R303) : Magma (Fin 9) :=
  Magma.mk (Magma.transport S9R303.E S9R303.tr v.1)

end Magma

/-! ### The source exhibits

`1` members of the class, chosen by greedy cover so that between them they model all `43` equations
that have a model in the class at all. Each check is `Magma.tupOK`: the tuple names a member of the
class. It is `decide!` rather than `decide` because the invariance test is `81` cells times the `36`
group elements, which the elaborator will not walk inside its heartbeat limit.
-/

def vdsrch9R3030 : Array Nat := #[0, 0, 3, 3]

def vsrch9R3030 : Magma.tup9R303 :=
  ⟨fun i ↦ ⟨vdsrch9R3030[i.1]! % 9, Nat.mod_lt _ (by decide)⟩, by decide!⟩
